

# ── commit message format ───────────────────────────────────────
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body: 2-3 short lines on why. The diff already shows "how">
#
# type (required)
#   feat      New feature (op, kernel, pass, executor feature, ...)
#   fix       Bug fix
#   refactor  Restructure without changing behavior
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   test      Add/modify tests
#   bench     Add/modify benchmark programs
#   docs      Documentation
#   build     CMake, build configuration
#   chore     Everything else (gitignore, scripts, formatting, ...)
#
# scope (optional): kernels, core, graph, executor, pass, memory, bench, tools ...
#
# Examples
#   feat(kernels): add naive gemm kernel
#   bench: compare chrono vs cudaEvent timing
#   refactor(core): move launch config into ExecContext
#
# Rules
#   - Write in English. Subject: 72 characters max, no trailing period
#   - Keep the body short (2-3 lines); details belong in code comments or docs
#   - One concept per commit. Every commit must build and pass tests
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
